      "updated": 1776774848326,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "For a fork array cool idea.\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int arr[5] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};\n    int size = 5;\n\n    printf(\"10 steps around the circular array:\\n\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n        printf(\"%d \", arr[i % size]);  // wrap around\n    }\n}\n\n\n\nThis is a ring buffer an array that loops around!!!",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "For a fork array cool idea.\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int arr[5] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};\n    int size = 5;\n\n    printf(\"10 steps around the circular array:\\n\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n        printf(\"%d \", arr[i % size]);  // wrap around\n    }\n}\n\n\n\nThis is a ring buffer an array that loops around!!!",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
